+ new line
Which theme
This template uses github-light and github-dark — two themes that belong together and whose
colours stay legible on both grounds. It is set on the Syntax highlighting plugin.

en/2-formatting/08-math/blocks.content:
Two dollar signs set the formula as a block of its own:
$$
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2} \, dx = \sqrt{\pi}
$$
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2} \, dx = \sqrt{\pi}
Aligned over several lines
$$
\begin{aligned}
a &amp;= b + c \\
  &amp;= d + e + f \\
  &amp;= g
\end{aligned}
$$
\begin{aligned}
a &amp;= b + c \\
  &amp;= d + e + f \\
  &amp;= g
\end{aligned}
The &amp; marks the place where the lines line up.
Matrices
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
1 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; 1
\end{pmatrix}
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
1 &amp; 0 \\
0 &amp; 1
\end{pmatrix}
Formulas that are too wide
f(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 + a_3 x^3 + a_4 x^4 + a_5 x^5 + a_6 x^6 + a_7 x^7 + a_8 x^8 + a_9 x^9
The same applies here: what is too wide scrolls inside itself instead of blowing up the column.
